<title>AUSTRALIA: FAI says insurance units sold for A$50 mln.</title>
<headline>FAI says insurance units sold for A$50 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>FAI Insurances Ltd said the sale of its New Zealand and Pacific Island insurance operations would raise A$50 million and deliver a profit above carrying value.  </p>
<p>Insurer MMI Ltd said earlier it would buy FAI's general insurance operations in New Zealand, Fiji and Papua New Guinea.</p>
<p>FAI said it had agreed on the sale because the offer price was significantly above the carrying value, and because it believed the funds could be used for growth in countries with far stronger economies.</p>
<p>The sale agreement would not affect its New Zealand consumer fiance company, alarm distribution company and property development company, FAI said.</p>
<p>The sale is expected to be completed in August.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
